progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog-146-	* Python 3 support!  (Thorsten E. Behrens, Anders Sundman)
progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog-147-	  PyCrypto now supports every version of Python from 2.1 through 3.2.
progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog-148-
progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog-149-	* Timing-attack countermeasures in _fastmath: When built against
progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog:150:	  libgmp version 5 or later, we use mpz_powm_sec instead of mpz_powm.
progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog-151-	  This should prevent the timing attack described by Geremy Condra at
progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog-152-	  PyCon 2011:
progress/R103/inputs/source_git/python-pycrypto/ChangeLog-153-	  http://blip.tv/pycon-us-videos-2009-2010-2011/pycon-2011-through-the-side-channel-timing-and-implementation-attacks-in-python-4897955
